TEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;First-order low-pass (RC): H(s) = 1 / (1 + sRC) = ωc / (s + ωc)\nτ = RC = 100 µs and fc = 1 / (2π RC) ≈ 1.59 kHz: one pole at s = −1/RC = −10 krad/s and no finite zero.\nStep: out rises as 1 − e^(−t/τ) (63 % at t = τ). Bode: −3 dB at fc and then −20 dB/decade; the phase goes from 0 to −90°.
